From 6b6d45eaa32092af68c14229416b3662d0a342de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Konrad Dybcio <konrad.dybcio@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Mar 2025 16:32:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 39/85] arm64: dts: qcom: hamoa: Add USB4 routers

The Hamoa platform features 3 custom USB4v1 (40 Gbps via a Gen3x2 link)
Host Routers. Each one of them is connected to a USB3.1 Gen2 controller
and a Gen1x16 PCIe RC.

Additionally, they are all connected to a DP crossbar, letting any of
the three USB4-capable (sans DP3) DPTX controllers be runtime muxed to
any of the two DPIN ports of either of the three USB4 host routers.

The host routers are also compatible with Thunderbolt 3 and newer.

Most designs pair the router with an on-board Parade PS8830 or PS8833
retimer to ensure signal integrity.

Describe them and connect the relevant protocol controllers.

Signed-off-by: Konrad Dybcio <konrad.dybcio@oss.qualcomm.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
